WEBVTT

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:04.980
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the World Champion, Dande…

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:10.110
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew…

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:15.260
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:33.760
Over 10,000?
There are that many participants?!

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:37.760
I’m fired up!

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:42.890
They’re not called the Pokémon <i>World</i>  Championships
for nothing! They’re insanely popular!

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:50.400
That’s fine! The more rivals,
the more excitement!

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.410
More and more keep
signing up after me!

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:58.660
I see… Everyone starts out
in the Normal Class, huh?

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:04.040
And above that is the Super Class, Hyper Class
and then the Master Class!

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.540
Everyone shares
the same starting line.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:10.800
Your momentum greatly depends on
whether you win or lose your first battle.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.600
The first battle is vital.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:13.670
Got it!

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:15.970
Right, let’s do this, Pikachu!

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:18.550
What are you gonna do?

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:23.620
If I wanna battle Mr. Dande,
then first of all I gotta enter the Super Class!

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:26.900
In which case,
there’s only one thing to do!

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:28.560
Win, win,
and win some more!

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:33.820
You fired up, too, Gänger?

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:36.580
It looks like the best way
to rapidly climb the ranks…

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:40.670
…is to fight someone
ranked much higher than yourself.

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:42.530
So basically, strong trainers?

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:46.610
I wonder if there are any
participating trainers nearby.

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:48.480
As strong as I can find!

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.540
You sure are impatient.

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.670
Look into it yourself!

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:54.170
Search for “Kuchiba City”.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:55.800
Oh, I see!

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:58.200
”Kuchiba City”…

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:00.370
Found one!

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.860
I choose this trainer!

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:05.140
Ranking number 2109…

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:09.360
Isn’t that the substitute
Gym Leader in Kuchiba Gym?

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:13.650
Kuchiba Gym? Wasn’t Matis
the Gym Leader there?

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:15.330
Exactly.

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:20.650
But I hear he’s out training right now,
trying to refine his mastery over the Electric type.

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:23.410
Out training…?

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:26.820
His substitute, Bisces,
is quite formidable as well!

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:29.300
Are you sure you should start
with such a high bar?

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:35.520
Now I’m <i>really</i>  fired up!

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:41.430
Satoshi is finally starting his
Pokémon World Championships challenge.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:43.210
His target is Dande!

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:45.810
All is for the sake of
becoming the strongest!

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:52.570
PocketMonsters

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:54.990
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:57.570
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:00.290
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:03.160
And skip the slow send-off

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.500
Be it through fire or through water

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.170
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:12.670
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:17.930
Each and every one of my memories

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:22.520
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:26.440
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:32.190
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:39.200
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:43.410
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:44.750
Let's have a fight!

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:47.460
1: Once the battle's done

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.290
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:53.630
On 3, let's be friends!

00:03:54.920 --> 00:04:00.300
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:05.640
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:08.140
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:12.270
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:14.070
I choose you!

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:23.070
The Pokémon World Championships!!
Satoshi Joins In!

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:29.940
Hey, do you have
Kuchiba Gym’s Badge?

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:30.710
Sure do!

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:34.210
I got it from Matis
after fighting his Raichu!

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:36.840
It was my third Badge!

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:41.810
The world has Pokémon Gyms
built in all sorts of locations.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:46.850
In them reside Gym Leaders,
whom many trainers look up to.

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:50.670
Challengers are tested
in their Pokémon battling skills,

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:53.850
and receive a Badge
if they are victorious.

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:58.820
But in the Pokémon World Championships
Satoshi is now entering,

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:03.090
Gym Leaders and normal trainers alike
all start in the Normal Class,

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:06.120
regardless of their prior careers.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:09.370
It’s an Onisuzume!

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:14.670
Sorry, Satoshi!
I got things to do!

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.200
Rabbifoot!

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:18.630
H-Hey, hang on!

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:24.130
Hang in there, Go!

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:28.390
Kuchiba Gym, Kanto Region

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:36.650
You are strong!
I commend you!

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:40.650
But you lack something vital
if you want to surpass us!

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:49.910
What do I speak of?
Answer me!

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:51.100
What?

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:52.160
Well…

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:55.450
Spirit!
The spirit to conquer yourself!

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:59.330
Gym Battles are all about
you challengers…

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:04.940
…showing the strength that you and your Pokémon
built up to us Gym Leaders through battle!

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:09.130
The Badge is the proof
that you have taken us down!

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:13.220
But I wish to commend
your battling prowess!

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:17.520
And so, we will bury you
with our strongest move.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:18.440
Volteccer!

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:36.040
Sleeper is unable to battle!

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:39.300
As such, Gym Leader substitute
Bisces wins!

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:42.800
I… I accept defeat!

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:45.670
Good. Train hard,
and challenge us again!

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:47.810
Your battling showed real promise.

00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:03.440
Well done, Deputy Captain!

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:05.940
That was the last
Gym challenger for the day.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:06.570
I see.

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:12.400
You fought well today.
You never let me down, Raichu.

00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:16.000
You still haven’t fought enough?

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:21.580
It would be nice if a trainer in the Championships
would show up right now.

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:26.950
Your current rank is 2109…

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:28.090
No change.

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:33.710
Is this…?

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:37.170
A Championships
participant is nearby!

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:40.940
Excuse me!

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:51.280
This is an official
battle announcement.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:53.950
I see. So it’s you.

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:56.450
Would you like to battle? Or not?

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:58.950
Of course I’ll battle!

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:00.710
I’m Satoshi from Masara Town!

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:04.740
I’d like to battle you, Bisces!

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:06.740
Very well!

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:09.880
Official battle appointment made!

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:13.010
Deputy Captain, this trainer is…

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:15.260
I didn’t expect
Satoshi from Masara Town…

00:08:18.650 --> 00:08:21.270
I wanted to meet you,
and your Pikachu as well.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:25.270
Captain Matis told me about…

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:32.850
…the young boy who once overcame
him and Raichu in a spectacular battle;

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:35.960
Satoshi from Masara Town
and his Pikachu.

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:46.680
This Raichu is my comrade,
trained by the Captain himself!

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:49.730
Satoshi!

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:51.730
I made it in time!

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:52.860
Go!

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:54.180
Who are you?

00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:57.390
This is my friend, Go!

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:59.370
He came to cheer me on
during the battle!

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:00.440
Nice to meet you!

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:01.930
Got the Onisuzume?

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:05.460
All right, you did it!

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:06.840
Yup!

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:09.500
And now it’s my turn to shine!

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:15.070
Bisces! I just entered the Championships,
and this will be my first battle!

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:19.660
I’m honored that you’d choose me
as your historic first opponent!

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:25.100
Welcome! Welcome!
Welcome!

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:30.490
The Pokémon World Championships
has approved this Normal Class battle!

00:09:30.490 --> 00:09:36.300
The battle will be between Kuchiba Gym’s Bisces
and Satoshi from Masara Town!

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:39.450
Happy to have you as judge again,
Drone Rotom!

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:42.860
Oh, a Drone Rotom?
Never seen one before!

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:43.640
Nice to meet’cha!

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:49.470
This battle will be a 2v2.

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:53.190
Now, allow me to explain
the official rules!

00:09:53.710 --> 00:09:56.450
You are free to switch Pokémon
during the battle.

00:09:56.450 --> 00:10:04.210
When all of a trainer’s Pokémon are incapacitated,
that trainer loses, and the trainer remaining wins!

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:09.710
And the battle judge will be myself,
as approved by the Championships!

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:12.210
What are those?

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:17.350
All right, both sides send out
your Pokémon at the same time.

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:18.390
3!

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:19.410
2!

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:20.380
1!

00:10:20.380 --> 00:10:20.830
Go!

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:22.100
Go, Raichu!
Pikachu, I choose you!

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:22.820
Pikachu, I choose you!

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:32.620
Raichu! Mouse Pokémon!
Electric type!

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:34.380
Pikachu’s evolved form!

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:39.450
As electricity builds up inside its body,
it becomes more aggressive!

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:42.240
Hang in there, Pikachu!

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:46.200
Battle start!

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:48.000
This is my squadron’s welcome!

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.460
100,000 Volts!

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:54.100
We’ll use 100,000 Volts, too!

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:03.760
Satoshi and Pikachu are both
going at full throttle!

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:07.600
Volteccer!

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:11.260
A Volteccer already?!

00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:12.730
They plan on finishing this
right away?

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:14.520
Pikachu! Iron Tail!

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:17.030
Stand on your tail!

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:24.330
That’s…

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:26.460
The tactic the Captain
was praising!

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:29.710
He’s discharging the power of Volteccer
into the ground!

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:34.090
And the power of Iron Tail is helping him
withstand the impact from Raichu’s tackle!

00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:35.670
Don’t give up, Pikachu!

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:37.970
Disperse all the electric power
into the battlefield!

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:52.060
Raichu!
Show them our power!

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:58.740
Pikachu!

00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:01.510
Brute force wasn’t enough, huh?

00:12:01.510 --> 00:12:02.200
Catch him!

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:07.080
Amazing!
Is that even possible?!

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:13.830
Hang in there, Pikachu!

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:15.290
Now, Raichu!

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:19.760
Iron Tail!

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:29.770
Reflector!

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:49.550
An impressive call…

00:12:49.550 --> 00:12:53.920
Raichu would have taken a lot of damage
if we hadn’t put up the Reflector in time.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:59.340
Turn every bad situation into a chance!
That’s how we’ve always fought!

00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:03.120
Don’t push yourself, Pikachu.
Return!

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:09.870
You did well.

00:13:11.510 --> 00:13:12.820
Gänger!

00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:15.520
I choose you!

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:26.220
PocketMonsters

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:28.220
Pocket Monsters!
PocketMonsters

00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:31.580
PocketMonsters

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:36.500
Electric
Raichu
PocketMonsters

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:38.460
It’s all on you, Gänger!

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:40.500
You can beat its tail!

00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:43.930
Can you go on, Raichu?

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:48.290
Gänger, huh…

00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:50.260
How will this battle go?

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:55.810
Now! Night Head!

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:00.270
100,000 Volts!

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:09.320
Ice Punch!

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:14.000
How can it move like that?!

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:17.160
Use your tail, Raichu!

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:22.800
What?!

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:29.620
I see! He took advantage of
Gänger’s intangibility!

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:35.690
Good, Gänger!
That tail isn’t scary at all!

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:38.190
Well then… Volteccer!

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:40.560
Psychokinesis!

00:14:44.810 --> 00:14:45.740
What?!

00:14:50.680 --> 00:14:51.810
Raichu!

00:14:58.440 --> 00:14:59.920
Raichu is unable to battle!

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:03.670
<i>The</i>  Raichu?!

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:05.740
You did it, Gänger!

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:13.020
I knew you could do it,
Satoshi!

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:15.990
You used Gänger’s unpredictable movement
to your advantage!

00:15:18.210 --> 00:15:19.510
Come back, Raichu.

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:23.280
You fought well.
I will avenge you.

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:28.400
I have my own way to
counter tricky movement!

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:31.660
Go, my squadron’s
ultimate lethal weapon!

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:37.830
Yes! Marumine!

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:42.580
Marumine! Ball Pokémon!
Electric type!

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:45.700
It explodes in response
to even minor stimuli!

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:49.380
It is feared, with the nickname of
“The Bomb Ball”!

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:51.120
This shape…

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:54.680
Electromagnetic Levitation!

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:03.360
That’s not the only thing we can do
with our Electromagnetic Levitation!

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:11.450
What is this?!

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:16.330
Most challengers counter the Electric type
with Ground-type moves!

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:20.890
The Electromagnetic Levitation we’ve developed
to counteract that can even control space!

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:23.820
Meaning,
Marumine has no rival!

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:27.340
Commence bombardment!

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:45.730
Gänger! Watch Marumine’s
movements carefully!

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:55.740
Those imprints on the wall
were from this attack!

00:16:55.740 --> 00:17:00.500
Good! Gänger can’t get out
of Marumine’s electric cage!

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:05.580
Above you!

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:15.360
Psychokinesis!

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:30.090
Gänger! Night Head!

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:32.650
Discharge!

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:40.990
Gänger!

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:46.500
Gänger is unable to battle!

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:57.310
Take a nice, long rest.

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:02.270
Counting on you, Pikachu!

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:07.730
Now it’s one on one…

00:18:09.110 --> 00:18:10.270
Let’s end this!

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:11.440
Marumine, use Rollout!

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:17.650
Pikachu!
Watch its movements carefully!

00:18:31.990 --> 00:18:33.820
Do something, Satoshi!

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:35.510
You’ll lose at this rate!

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:40.640
My Marumine’s attacks deal more damage
the more it gets to accelerate!

00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:43.470
How long can Pikachu last?!

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:46.170
In that case…

00:18:46.170 --> 00:18:49.350
Pikachu! Get on top of Marumine
and use Iron Tail!

00:18:58.610 --> 00:18:59.570
He stopped it!

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:02.410
Good, Pikachu!
Now, spin it in reverse!

00:19:07.710 --> 00:19:09.210
How is this…

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:11.100
That’s insane, Satoshi…

00:19:14.060 --> 00:19:16.130
He took control of Marumine!

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:17.590
What an insult!

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:20.800
Finish it off! Iron Tail!

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:31.230
No way!

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:32.110
Sympathetic Detonation?!

00:19:32.860 --> 00:19:34.510
Wait, Marumine!

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:36.820
Electroweb!

00:19:44.920 --> 00:19:47.640
I… I can’t believe it…

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:54.750
Well done, Pikachu!

00:19:57.290 --> 00:20:00.260
Marumine is unable to battle!
Pikachu wins!

00:20:02.620 --> 00:20:05.770
As such, the winner is
Satoshi from Masara Town!

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:08.310
All right!

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:16.910
They triggered your ability,
Sympathetic Detonation…

00:20:16.910 --> 00:20:19.820
You must have battled
past your own limits.

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:28.200
I stand defeated.

00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:30.660
Bisces!

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:33.360
I’ll report this to Captain Matis!

00:20:33.360 --> 00:20:37.670
I’m sure he’ll want to battle
this new and stronger you, too!

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:40.050
I’d love to battle Matis…

00:20:40.620 --> 00:20:42.430
To battle the Captain again, too!

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:46.030
